eduction test works, and whether itemizing saves you more money.","og:image":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon-192.png","og:site_name":"ModernWallet","og:title":"Tax Deductions for Homeowners and the Itemizing Test in 2026","og:type":"website","og:url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/tax-deductions-for-homeowners/","twitter:card":"summary_large_image","twitter:description":"Learn which tax deductions for homeowners qualify in 2026, how the standard deduction test works, and whether itemizing saves you more money.","twitter:image":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon-192.png","twitter:title":"Tax Deductions for Homeowners and the Itemizing Test in 2026","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},"schema":[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@id":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/#organization","@type":"Organization","description":"Free, accurate financial calculators — auto loans, mortgages, retirement, investing, rentals, and net worth. No signup, instant results.","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon.svg"},"name":"ModernWallet","parentOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Layer3Labs","url":"https://www.layer3labs.io"},"url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@id":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/#website","@type":"WebSite","description":"Free, accurate financial calculators — auto loans, mortgages, retirement, investing, rentals, and net worth. No signup, instant results.","name":"ModernWallet","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/","name":"ModernWallet","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/","name":"Guides","position":2},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/tax-deductions-for-homeowners/","name":"Tax Deductions for Homeowners in 2026","position":3}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, mortgage interest is deductible on acquisition debt up to $750,000 for single and joint filers, or $375,000 for married individuals filing separately, for homes acquired after December 15, 2017. You must itemize deductions on Schedule A to claim it, and loans originating before December 16, 2017, qualify under an older $1 million limit."},"name":"Is mortgage interest tax deductible in 2026?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, state and local property taxes are deductible on Schedule A, subject to the combined state and local tax deduction cap. For 2025, that cap is $40,000, or $20,000 for married filers filing separately, with a statutory floor of $10,000 and an annual 1% increase that makes the cap $40,400 for 2026."},"name":"Are property taxes deductible?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can deduct interest on a home equity loan or line of credit only if the borrowed money was used to buy, build, or substantially improve the home securing the loan. If the funds were used for other purposes, such as paying down personal loans or funding college tuition, the interest is not deductible."},"name":"Can I deduct home equity loan or HELOC interest?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Standard home renovations and routine repairs are not deductible, but medically necessary modifications may qualify under Schedule A medical expense deductions. The deductible amount is restricted to the cost that exceeds any increase in the market value of your property, and total medical expenses must surpass 7.5% of your adjusted gross income."},"name":"Can I deduct home improvements?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You should itemize only if your total qualifying deductions, including mortgage interest, property taxes, poi